<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Home-screen sizes, in the launcher's own grid units.

  Every value is `70 × cells − 30` dp, the conversion the App Widget sizing
  guide gives for turning a cell count into the `minWidth` / `minHeight` a
  provider declares (developer.android.com/develop/ui/views/appwidgets
  § "Determine widget sizing"):

      1 cell → 40dp    2 cells → 110dp    3 cells → 180dp
      4 cells → 250dp  5 cells → 320dp

  These are PLACEMENT sizes only — the default each provider asks for and the
  range a launcher may resize it within. They are NOT breakpoints: both widgets
  use `SizeMode.Exact`, so the balance card lays out for the height it is
  actually given (`balanceCardContent`) rather than for the nearest of a
  declared set.
-->
<resources>
  <!--
    The balance widget. Default placement 4 cells wide by 3 tall.

    THREE tall rather than two, and the number came out of the arithmetic in
    `WalletWidgetStyle.kt` rather than out of taste. The actions row is a 48dp
    tap target — Material's minimum, so it cannot be shaved — plus its 8dp gap,
    and the whole design (Pocket, balance, fiat, stamp, actions) does not fit
    under about 180dp. A 2-cell default would therefore have shipped a card with
    no shortcuts on it for everyone who never resized, which is most people.
    At 3 cells the full design fits whenever nothing is pending, and the pending
    line displaces the shortcuts on the rare card that needs it.
  -->
  <dimen name="fairwallet_balance_widget_min_width">250dp</dimen>
  <dimen name="fairwallet_balance_widget_min_height">180dp</dimen>

  <!--
    It may be dragged down to 2 cells wide and ONE tall, where it still has a
    form worth showing: the balance and its stamp, with everything else shed.
    60dp rather than 40dp because two lines of type — a 24sp balance and an 11sp
    stamp, each occupying about 1.3× its size in a TextView, inside 12dp of
    padding — come to a little under it, and a `minResizeHeight` is a floor a
    launcher measures a drag against rather than a size the widget is ever
    given, so it does not have to be a whole number of cells.
  -->
  <dimen name="fairwallet_balance_widget_min_resize_width">110dp</dimen>
  <dimen name="fairwallet_balance_widget_min_resize_height">60dp</dimen>

  <!--
    The ceiling: 5×5 is where the card runs out of things to reveal, so a larger
    placement would only stretch what is already there.
  -->
  <dimen name="fairwallet_balance_widget_max_resize_width">320dp</dimen>
  <dimen name="fairwallet_balance_widget_max_resize_height">320dp</dimen>

  <!--
    The actions widget. Two buttons side by side and nothing else, so it asks
    for 2 cells by 1 and never needs to grow: its height ceiling is the same
    single cell it starts at, because a 48dp pill centred in a 250dp-tall widget
    would be a lot of empty green.
  -->
  <dimen name="fairwallet_actions_widget_min_width">110dp</dimen>
  <dimen name="fairwallet_actions_widget_min_height">40dp</dimen>
  <dimen name="fairwallet_actions_widget_min_resize_width">110dp</dimen>
  <dimen name="fairwallet_actions_widget_min_resize_height">40dp</dimen>
  <dimen name="fairwallet_actions_widget_max_resize_width">320dp</dimen>
  <dimen name="fairwallet_actions_widget_max_resize_height">110dp</dimen>
</resources>
